/*
 * Board overlay for the Sakura Board VM.
 *
 * LEDs / button / serial work from the board's default devicetree, so for a first
 * `west build` you may not need anything here.
 *
 * The buzzer uses PWM. To make `tone` beep, enable a PWM node and route the buzzer
 * pin to one of its channels, then set its label to `pwm0` (or adjust hal_zephyr.cpp).
 * Example shape (fill in the real pin for your board):
 *
 *   &pwm0 {
 *       status = "okay";
 *       pinctrl-0 = <&pwm0_default>;
 *       pinctrl-names = "default";
 *   };
 *
 * See the nRF Connect SDK PWM samples and your board's .dts for the exact syntax.
 */
